__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
logs.txt
experiments.txt
# Codabench submission zips are results, not build artifacts -- they are the only thing a
# teammate can actually submit, and every Qwen run folder tracks one. A local `*.zip` rule
# in .git/info/exclude was silently dropping them. .gitignore takes precedence over
# info/exclude, so this negation keeps them tracked.
#
# The glob is deliberately loose. An earlier exact `prediction_en.zip` stopped matching the
# moment a file was renamed (prediction_en_DEV.zip, to keep a dev run from being clobbered
# by its devtest re-run) and the *.zip rule quietly ate it again -- no error, no warning.
!**/prediction_en*.zip
experiments.txt